<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xie An</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">320–385</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xie An was a Chinese statesman of the Eastern Jin dynasty and head of the aristocratic Xie clan. Long a celebrated recluse, he entered office in his forties, became chief minister and checked the ambitions of the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huan-wen">Huan Wen</a>. When Fu Jian of the Former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> invaded in 383, he directed the defence in which his relatives <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xie-shi">Xie Shi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xie-xuan">Xie Xuan</a> won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-river">Battle of Fei River</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xie-an.jpg" alt="Xie An" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GnuDoyng · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_xie_an.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
